eous_phase":"phosphate buffer","pH":7.01,"temperature_C":25,"doi":"10.1002/ejic.201601129","year":2017,"counterion":"F[P-](F)(F)(F)(F)F","record_id":"MLDB-000197","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"The lipophilicity of each complex of the series (Log Po/w) was experimentally determined by the “shake-flask” method. Briefly, an aliquot of a stock solution of the iridium complex was diluted in the phosphate buffer (pH = 7.01, saturated with 1-octanol), and then the same volume of 1-octanol (previously saturated by the phosphate buffer) was added. Then, the mixture was shaken at 80 rpm for 12 h at 298 K to allow full distribution. After centrifugation at 2500 rpm for 5 min, the octanol layer was carefully removed. The Ir concentration in the aqueous phase was determined by ICP-MS after digestion of the aqueous phase with 65 % HNO3 for one day. The data was used to calculate the Log Po/w values by using the relevant equation in the literature.23"}]}